<p class="standfirst">
  Long essays on where this came from: the ideas, the people and the
  machines that led to AI, and the arguments that were had about them at
  the time. Written for a reader who is clever and not a specialist. Every
  claim of fact carries a footnote to a source you can open. Before
  anything here is published, a second machine that had no part in the
  writing checks the footnotes and says what it found; its report is at the
  foot of each essay. Nothing is made up. If something is wrong, the page
  says so when it is found.
</p>

{%- if collections.history.length %}
<ul class="index">
{%- for essay in collections.history %}
  <li>
    <a href="{{ essay.url | url }}">{{ essay.data.title }}</a>
    <span class="eyebrow">{{ essay.date | readable }}{% if essay.data.reading_time %} · {{ essay.data.reading_time }}{% endif %}</span>
    {%- if essay.data.standfirst %}<span class="eyebrow">{{ essay.data.standfirst }}</span>{% endif %}
  </li>
{%- endfor %}
</ul>
{%- else %}
<p>The first essay is being checked.</p>
{%- endif %}
